          "content": "**Guiding question:** Which thermodynamic forces enable corrosion and what can potentials establish without claiming a rate?\n\nA mixed-metal water-handling assembly fails soon after a new fitting is introduced. Determine whether the available evidence supports galvanic interaction, deposit-related aeration, or an unrelated design fault. The investigation begins with a defined material and state, a particular environment and the time-dependent physical response. Distinguish metal-dissolution, oxide formation, product transport and structural weakening rather than compressing all visible changes into one category. Separate a possible reaction from a verified rate and a local failure mode from an area-averaged measurement. For this unit, a useful answer must identify an observable that would falsify a favored account and an independent observation that constrains the competing mechanism. Neither ideal electrochemical equations nor visual inspection alone resolves all ambiguities.",
