          "heading": "System view and mechanism boundaries",
          "content": "**Guiding question:** How do charge transfer, transport, and instrumental resistance shape the observed corrosion response?\n\nTwo electrodes have similar measured open-circuit potentials but exhibit very different mass loss. Establish a defensible test program before assigning corrosion rates. The investigation begins with a defined material and state, a particular environment and the time-dependent physical response. Distinguish metal-dissolution, oxide formation, product transport and structural weakening rather than compressing all visible changes into one category. Separate a possible reaction from a verified rate and a local failure mode from an area-averaged measurement. For this unit, a useful answer must identify an observable that would falsify a favored account and an independent observation that constrains the competing mechanism. Neither ideal electrochemical equations nor visual inspection alone resolves all ambiguities.",
