          "content": "**Guiding question:** What creates a protective surface film and when can manufacturing history defeat it?\n\nA welded stainless-steel vessel exhibits attack near the weld rather than across its smooth parent plate. Separate chemistry, microstructure and service causes. The investigation begins with a defined material and state, a particular environment and the time-dependent physical response. Distinguish metal-dissolution, oxide formation, product transport and structural weakening rather than compressing all visible changes into one category. Separate a possible reaction from a verified rate and a local failure mode from an area-averaged measurement. For this unit, a useful answer must identify an observable that would falsify a favored account and an independent observation that constrains the competing mechanism. Neither ideal electrochemical equations nor visual inspection alone resolves all ambiguities.",
