          "content": "**Guiding question:** When do protective scales slow oxidation, and when do thermal cycling or reactive gases change the mechanism?\n\nA furnace part loses strength after hundreds of hot cycles. Determine which observations distinguish oxide growth, scale spallation and mechanical fatigue. The investigation begins with a defined material and state, a particular environment and the time-dependent physical response. Distinguish metal-dissolution, oxide formation, product transport and structural weakening rather than compressing all visible changes into one category. Separate a possible reaction from a verified rate and a local failure mode from an area-averaged measurement. For this unit, a useful answer must identify an observable that would falsify a favored account and an independent observation that constrains the competing mechanism. Neither ideal electrochemical equations nor visual inspection alone resolves all ambiguities.",
