          "secNumber": "7.1",
          "heading": "System view and mechanism boundaries",
          "content": "**Guiding question:** How can a test result support a real operating decision rather than become a misleading laboratory number?\n\nAn accelerated test ranks two candidate materials opposite to their field history. Design an evidence audit, sampling program, and cautious decision. The investigation begins with a defined material and state, a particular environment and the time-dependent physical response. Distinguish metal-dissolution, oxide formation, product transport and structural weakening rather than compressing all visible changes into one category. Separate a possible reaction from a verified rate and a local failure mode from an area-averaged measurement. For this unit, a useful answer must identify an observable that would falsify a favored account and an independent observation that constrains the competing mechanism. Neither ideal electrochemical equations nor visual inspection alone resolves all ambiguities.",
